Purpose: non-final inventory/manifest preview for independent correction reviews; not the active assets.sha256 and not a package-integrity pass.
Declared scope: all regular files recursively under r4 except r4/assets.sha256 and the three pre-registered external PA/R2/R4 post-manifest attestation report paths; plus every regular path in r4/assets-outside-paths.txt.
Generation: sorted SHA-256 entries relative to repository root. Reject symlink/special files in r4 scope, absent/non-regular explicit outside paths, duplicates, or any active manifest entry under build/.
The preview itself is copied into r4 after generation and is included in the eventual final manifest. This preview does not list itself, the superseded active assets.sha256, or the three attestation reports; the final assets.sha256 will list every regular r4 file except itself and the three exact attestation reports, including assets-preview.sha256 and this generation log.
Attempt 1: inventory check aborted before writing a preview because the ad-hoc type-check branch incorrectly classified the intentionally excluded regular `assets.sha256` as a special file. No active manifest or evidence was modified. Corrected the branch to distinguish regular-but-excluded from special files before retrying; retain this failed attempt for transparency.
Post-review inventory update: the initial 157-entry preview was generated with 37 explicit outside paths and before assets-preview.sha256 was copied into r4. PA, V&V/R2 and R4 inventory-correction reports, followed by the R2 candidate-identity delta report, were produced afterward and added to assets-outside-paths.txt; that list now contains 41 paths. Consequently the initial preview and the old active assets.sha256 are not the current complete inventory. Regenerate after controlled status/index updates and final reports are frozen; the final manifest must include the preview file, this updated log, all four correction reports, and the current outside list.
